{%- liquid
  assign p1 = section.settings.product_single
  assign p2 = section.settings.product_two
  assign p4 = section.settings.product_four
  assign v1 = p1.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign v2 = p2.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign v4 = p4.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign wired = false
  if v1 != blank and v2 != blank and v4 != blank
    assign wired = true
  endif
  comment
    Prices shown when a tier has no product connected yet. Once a product is
    picked in the editor its real price and compare-at price take over.
  endcomment
  assign m1 = '$34.99'
  if v1
    assign m1 = v1.price | money
  endif
  assign m2 = '$59.99'
  if v2
    assign m2 = v2.price | money
  endif
  assign picked = 2
-%}
<!-- ============ 1. product hero ============ -->
<section class="pdp" id="buy">
  <div class="wrap pdp__grid">

    <!-- gallery -->
    <div class="gal">
      <div class="gal__stage">
        <button class="gal__arrow gal__arrow--prev" type="button" data-gal="-1" aria-label="Previous image">&#8249;</button>
        <button class="gal__arrow gal__arrow--next" type="button" data-gal="1" aria-label="Next image">&#8250;</button>
        <ul class="gal__reel" data-gal-reel>

          <li class="gal__slide is-on">
            <img src="{{ 'balm-one.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="One PDRN Pink Collagen Volume Multi Balm beside its carton" width="1024" height="1024">
          </li>

          <li class="gal__slide">
            <img src="{{ 'balm-two.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Two multi balm sticks, each beside its carton" width="1024" height="1024">
          </li>

          <li class="gal__slide">
            <img src="{{ 'balm-four.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Four multi balm sticks standing on a warm taupe backdrop" width="1024" height="1024">
          </li>

          <li class="gal__slide">
            <img src="{{ 'application-closeup.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="A woman gliding the pink multi balm along her cheekbone, the balm visible on the skin" width="537" height="672">
          </li>

          <li class="gal__slide gal__slide--fit">
            <img src="{{ 'benefits-chart.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Chart of the balm's six benefits: deep hydration, smoothing fine lines, PDRN renewal, barrier support, multi area care, and portability" width="1024" height="1280">
          </li>

        </ul>
      </div>
      <ol class="gal__dots" data-gal-dots aria-label="Choose an image"></ol>
    </div>

    <!-- buy column -->
    <div class="pdp__info">
      <p class="kicker">N&deg; 1 &middot; The Pink Balm</p>
      <h1 class="pdp__title">The balm that goes<br>where cream won't.</h1>
      <p class="pdp__lede">Built for women who are done with a seven step routine. This is one step, and it takes eleven seconds.</p>

      <ul class="chips">
        <li class="chip">Fine lines</li>
        <li class="chip">Eye area</li>
        <li class="chip">Smile lines</li>
        <li class="chip chip--alt">Neck &amp; d&eacute;collet&eacute;</li>
        <li class="chip chip--alt">Lip barrier</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="panel" id="pricing">
        <p class="panel__head">PDRN Pink Collagen Volume Multi Balm &middot; 10 g &middot; About 45 days</p>

        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>5% PDRN, printed on the tube, not hidden inside a blend</li>
          <li>Glides straight over makeup. No fingers, no mess, no waiting</li>
          <li>One stick for the eye area, smile lines, neck and lips</li>
          <li>Full ingredient list and batch number on every carton</li>
          <li>30 days from delivery to change your mind, used or not</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="tiers" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Choose your quantity">
          {%- for n in (1..3) -%}
            {%- case n -%}
              {%- when 1 -%}
                {%- assign tv = v1 -%}{%- assign count = 1 -%}{%- assign fp = 3499 -%}{%- assign fc = 4599 -%}
                {%- assign tname = 'One stick' -%}{%- assign tsub = 'Try it on one side of your face first' -%}
              {%- when 2 -%}
                {%- assign tv = v2 -%}{%- assign count = 2 -%}{%- assign fp = 5999 -%}{%- assign fc = 7499 -%}
                {%- assign tname = 'Two sticks' -%}{%- assign tsub = 'One for home, one for your bag. About three months' -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign tv = v4 -%}{%- assign count = 4 -%}{%- assign fp = 10599 -%}{%- assign fc = 14309 -%}
                {%- assign tname = 'Four sticks' -%}{%- assign tsub = 'Six months of it, bought once' -%}
            {%- endcase -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign price = fp
              assign was = fc
              if tv
                assign price = tv.price
                assign was = tv.compare_at_price | default: 0
              endif
            -%}

          <label class="tier{% if count == picked %} is-picked{% endif %}">
            <input type="radio" name="qty" value="{{ count }}" data-slide="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
              {%- if count == picked %} checked{% endif %}
              {%- if tv %} data-variant="{{ tv.id }}"{% endif %} data-money="{{ price | money }}">
            {%- if count == 2 %}
            <span class="tier__flag">Most loved</span>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- if count > 1 and was > price %}
            <span class="tier__save">Save {{ was | minus: price | money }}</span>
            {%- endif %}
            <span class="tier__body">
              <span class="tier__name">{{ tname }}</span>
              <span class="tier__sub">{{ tsub }}</span>
              <span class="tier__fine">
                {%- if count > 1 -%}
                  {{ price | divided_by: count | money }} each &middot; free shipping
                {%- else -%}
                  Free shipping
                {%- endif %} &middot; 6 to 12 working days</span>
            </span>
            <span class="tier__cost">
              <b>{{ price | money }}</b>
              {%- if was > price %}<s>{{ was | money }}</s>{% endif -%}
            </span>
          </label>
          {%- endfor %}

        </div>

        <button class="btn btn--fill btn--wide" type="button" data-atc>Add to bag &middot; {{ m2 }}</button>
        {%- if request.design_mode and wired == false %}
        <p class="fine" style="color:var(--wine)">Pick a product for each bundle in this section's settings to turn on checkout.</p>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if request.design_mode %}
        {%- comment -%} theme editor only: what Shopify reports for the variant each tier adds {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="diag">
          <p class="diag__h">Theme editor only &middot; not shown to shoppers</p>
          {%- assign tier_names = 'One stick,Two sticks,Four sticks' | split: ',' -%}
          {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
            {%- case forloop.index -%}
              {%- when 1 -%}{%- assign dp = p1 -%}{%- assign dv = v1 -%}
              {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign dp = p2 -%}{%- assign dv = v2 -%}
              {%- else -%}{%- assign dp = p4 -%}{%- assign dv = v4 -%}
            {%- endcase -%}
            <p class="diag__row{% unless dv.available %} diag__row--bad{% endunless %}">
              <b>{{ tier_names[forloop.index0] }}:</b>
              {% if dp == blank -%}
                no product, or it is not published to the Online Store
              {%- else -%}
                {{ dp.title }} (/products/{{ dp.handle }}) &middot; variant {{ dv.id }}{% if dp.variants.size > 1 %} of {{ dp.variants.size }}{% endif %}
                &middot; {% if dv.available %}can be sold{% else %}SOLD OUT{% endif %}
                &middot; out of stock: {% if dv.inventory_policy == 'continue' %}continue selling{% else %}stop selling{% endif %}
                &middot; {% if dv.inventory_management == blank %}quantity not tracked{% else %}{{ dv.inventory_quantity }} in stock{% endif %}
              {%- endif %}
            </p>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        {%- endif %}

        <ul class="assure">
          <li><span class="assure__ico" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>30 day guarantee</li>
          <li><span class="assure__ico" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>Free shipping</li>
          <li><span class="assure__ico" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>6 to 12 working days</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="acc" id="details">
        <details class="acc__item">
          <summary>The full ingredient list</summary>
          <div class="acc__body">
            <p>Every ingredient, in order, at the strength we use it. Nothing is grouped under a proprietary name.</p>
            <p><b>Sodium DNA (PDRN) 5%</b>, Hydrogenated Polyisobutene, Hydrolyzed Collagen, Sodium Hyaluronate, Niacinamide 2%, Ceramide NP, Panthenol, Squalane, Shea Butter, Candelilla Wax, Tocopherol, Rosa Damascena Flower Extract, Mica, CI 77491.</p>
            <p class="fine">The pink is mica and iron oxide. It sheers out clear on skin and leaves no colour behind.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="acc__item">
          <summary>How to use it</summary>
          <div class="acc__body">
            <p>Morning or night, on clean or made up skin. Twist up two millimetres, no more. Glide once under each eye, once along each smile line, once up the neck. Press in with two fingers for five seconds.</p>
            <p>It layers over serum and under sunscreen, and it will not pill under foundation as long as you press rather than rub.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="acc__item">
          <summary>Why PDRN, and not another peptide</summary>
          <div class="acc__body">
            <p>PDRN is a fragment of DNA taken from salmon milt. In Korea it has been used in clinics for years, and it has spent the last two of them moving into topicals. It is included here at 5%, which is the upper end of what a balm base can carry while staying stable.</p>
            <p>Peptides are not the enemy. We use collagen and niacinamide alongside it. PDRN is simply the one we built the formula around, and we would rather say that plainly than call it a complex.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="acc__item">
          <summary>Who this is not for</summary>
          <div class="acc__body">
            <p>If you have a salmon or fish allergy, skip it. PDRN is salmon derived and we will not tell you the amount is too small to matter.</p>
            <p>If you are on prescription retinoids or mid course with a dermatologist, ask them first. If you want an overnight change, this is not it, and no balm is.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="acc__item">
          <summary>Shipping, returns and the guarantee</summary>
          <div class="acc__body">
            <p>Shipping is free on every order, with no minimum. Delivery takes 6 to 12 working days.</p>
            <p>Returns run on the same clock as the guarantee: 30 days from the day your order arrives, so time in transit does not count against you. Inside that window, used or unused, email us and we refund it in full. After 30 days from delivery the order is no longer eligible, so if you are unsure, start the conversation early rather than late.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

