<!-- ============ 6. timeline ============ -->
<section class="weeks" id="weeks">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker center">What to expect</p>
    <h2 class="h2 center">Your first eight weeks.</h2>
    <p class="lede center">A balm is not an injection. Here is the honest version of what happens, and roughly when.</p>

    <ul class="week3">
      <li class="wcard">
        <p class="wcard__when">Week one &middot; Days 1 to 7</p>
        <h3 class="wcard__h">It feels like something</h3>
        <p>Cushion under the eye within about a minute, and it is still there when you wash your face at night. This part is the hyaluronic acid and the balm base, and it is the fastest thing the stick does.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="wcard">
        <p class="wcard__when">Weeks two to four</p>
        <h3 class="wcard__h">Makeup stops settling</h3>
        <p>The tell most women report first is not the mirror, it is concealer. It stops sinking into the lines under the eye by mid afternoon. Nothing has changed structurally. The surface is simply holding water.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="wcard">
        <p class="wcard__when">Weeks five to eight</p>
        <h3 class="wcard__h">Photographs change first</h3>
        <p>Softer, less shadowed, is what you are looking for, and it shows up in pictures before it shows up in the bathroom mirror. Take one now, at the same window, and compare at week eight.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="center"><a class="btn btn--fill" href="#pricing" data-pick="2">Take the eight weeks &middot; {{ m2 }}</a>
    <p class="fine">Two sticks. Free shipping. 30 day guarantee.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

