<!-- ============ 11. faq ============ -->
<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap faq__grid">

    <aside class="faq__aside">
      <p class="kicker">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Before you<br>add it to the bag.</h2>
      <p class="faq__note">The ones women actually email us, answered the way we would answer them in person.</p>
      <div class="faq__card">
        <p class="faq__card-h">Not covered here?</p>
        <p>Write to <a href="mailto:hello@lapeaurosee.com">hello@lapeaurosee.com</a> and a person replies, usually the same day. Our goal is to have you looking the best you have ever looked, so ask us anything before you buy.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="faq__list">

      <details class="qa" open>
        <summary>How long until I see anything?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>Cushion and comfort within a minute, on day one. That part is the balm base and the hyaluronic acid, and it is immediate.</p>
          <p>The change most women notice first arrives around week three, and it is usually concealer sitting better rather than anything in the mirror. Softer and less shadowed shows up in photographs by week eight. If you want a result in seven days, this is not it, and neither is anything else in a tube.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>Can I use it with retinol or tretinoin?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>Yes, and plenty of women use it precisely because they are on one. Apply the retinoid first, let it dry, then glide the balm over the top. The ceramide and squalane help with the flaking and tightness that come with the first few months.</p>
          <p>If you are mid course with a dermatologist, ask them before adding anything. They know your skin and we do not.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>Is it safe in pregnancy or while nursing?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>Nothing in the formula sits on the standard avoid list. No retinoids and no salicylic acid. That said, we are not the ones who should tell you it is fine. Show the ingredient list to your midwife or doctor and let them make the call.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>I have a fish allergy. Can I use it?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>No. PDRN is derived from salmon milt, and we will not tell you the amount is too small to matter. Skip this one.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>Will it pill under makeup?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>Not if you press instead of rub. Twist up no more than two millimetres, glide it on, then press it in with two fingers for about five seconds. Rubbing is what rolls a balm into little beads, and that is true of every balm, not only this one.</p>
          <p>It also goes on over finished makeup, which is why most people keep one in a bag rather than a bathroom.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>Is the pink going to show on my skin?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>No. The colour is mica and iron oxide, and it sheers out completely as you press it in. No tint, no shimmer, no cast, including on deeper skin tones. The stick is pink because the PDRN is, and we saw no reason to bleach it.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>How long does one stick last?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>About forty five days used once daily across the eye area, smile lines, neck and lips. Twice a day brings that closer to three weeks. Ten grams goes further than it looks, because a stick lays down a far thinner layer than fingers do.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>Why PDRN, and why only 5%?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>Five percent is the upper end of what a balm base carries while staying smooth. Push past it and the stick turns grainy and drags, which is why most brands quietly use far less and never print the number.</p>
          <p>Peptides are not the enemy, and we use collagen and niacinamide alongside it. PDRN is simply what the formula is built around, and we would rather say that plainly than call it a complex.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>What does the batch number get me?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>Type the number printed on your carton into the site and you get the certificate for your specific stick. Fill date, actives at their measured levels, stability results. Not a generic PDF written once for the whole product line.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>Shipping, returns and the guarantee</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>Shipping is free on every order, with no minimum. Delivery takes 6 to 12 working days.</p>
          <p>Returns run on the same clock as the guarantee: 30 days from the day your order arrives, so time in transit does not count against you. Inside that window, used or unused, email us and we refund it in full. After 30 days from delivery the order is no longer eligible, so if you are unsure, start the conversation early rather than late.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="qa">
        <summary>Is it tested on animals? Where is it made?</summary>
        <div class="qa__body">
          <p>No animal testing, and we do not sell anywhere that requires it. Formulated and filled in South Korea, in a facility that has been making PDRN topicals since well before the ingredient reached the West.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

